    "title": "A=1 first-degree ambient defect factorization",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "boundary restriction isomorphism and rowwise quotient divisor",
    "statement": "For each of the six A=1 profiles at e=ceil((rho-1)/3), the pole-absorbing three-contact product extends uniquely to a nonzero ambient biform A_j of bidegree (d-3,j), j in {0,1,2}. At every residual domain row x, the missing-root factor Qbar(x)/gcd(Qbar(x),H), of degree c_x=e-d_x, divides A_j(x). Hence every row with c_x>j is a common split X-factor of all coefficients of A_j; after removing their product, all remaining row deficits are at most j and divide the residual specialization.",
